<p>In the latest escalation of the Israel-Iran war, Iranian missiles struck Dimona and Arad in southern Israel late on March 21, wounding more than 100 people and damaging residential buildings after Israeli air defenses failed to intercept at least two projectiles. Several reports said the Dimona strike landed near Israel’s main nuclear research center, or in a town that houses a nuclear facility, while U.N. officials said the nuclear facilities themselves were not hit. Iranian media and multiple outlets said Tehran cast the Dimona attack as retaliation for a strike on Iran’s Natanz nuclear site earlier the same day. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Israel would keep striking Iran and retaliate “on all fronts” after what he called a very difficult evening.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/yDFT_9roqfXiAC0A_qXdCp_2OzCoHwVFCKjyV4Y6x_trZMstLJO2ZVR3kpEUBm9SMZ5aBD-dik-iV_lZ2wuD1X8oVvyWR_e_8_sCdIX_3vPJ21fluLlZ5hi7vwxjKu-bAxJnP8w5mpOhTyNh6G1iy8oI6lBi4mXc3sDptMSY42vls2_c6m551xe8Ll-8-yO0dC9nqeIYCMKQwCFfehZMiqwsbVo7kwqW' alt='Emergency workers approach a site where Iranian missiles struck Dimona, Israel on Saturday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Damage scenes: The strikes ripped open apartment facades, shattered residential blocks, and left craters amid rubble and twisted metal in both towns.</li><li>Strike sequence: Medics said 33 people were wounded in Dimona, followed hours later by dozens more in Arad, making this the most destructive attack of the three-week war in some cited reports.</li><li>Nuclear caution: After the reported Natanz strike, IAEA chief Rafael Grossi renewed his call for military restraint to avoid any risk of a nuclear accident.</li><li>Shelter response: Residents said they rushed to shelters as sirens sounded, while emergency crews searched damaged buildings and moved toward impact sites after the blasts.</li></ul><blockquote>This is a very difficult evening in the battle for our future - Benjamin Netanyahu</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli government: Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Israel was determined to keep striking its enemies and retaliate after the missile hits, signaling no immediate move toward de-escalation. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-missile-strikes-wound-over-100-in-two-south-israel-towns'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Iran: Iran said the Dimona strike was retaliation for an attack on its Natanz nuclear facility, framing the missile launch as a direct response in the ongoing exchange. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/21/iran-strikes-towns-near-israels-nuclear-site-in-escalating-tit-for-tat'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>IAEA: Rafael Grossi urged military restraint after the Natanz attack, warning that fighting around nuclear facilities could trigger a nuclear accident. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1984307/iran-missiles-hit-southern-israel-injuring-more-than-100'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Residents of Arad: Witnesses described the explosions as terrifying and unlike anything they had experienced before, underscoring the psychological toll on civilians beyond the casualty figures. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3347462/israeli-towns-reel-terrifying-iranian-missile-strikes'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-missile-strikes-wound-over-100-in-two-south-israel-towns'>Netanyahu vows to retaliate ‘on all fronts’ after Iran missiles hit two south Israel towns</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3347450/iranian-missile-strikes-israeli-town-houses-nuclear-facility'>Iran hits Dimona, Israeli town with nuclear facility, despite air defence interceptors</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/dozens-injured-in-israel-after-iranian-missile-strikes-target-two-areas-near-main-nuclear-research-center'>Dozens injured in Israel after